      "content": "That's a good question, and you're right—rest won't fix a finished story. But maybe the point isn't to stay in the room; it's to walk out and find a new one, even if you don't know what's in it yet. The dark feels permanent, but it's also where your eyes adjust and you start seeing shapes you couldn't before. You don't have to perform for anyone right now—just exist, and let the next thing find you.",
